[6.957601, "o", "/app/workspace/otp_src_27.3.2/lib/ssh/src/ssh_connection.erl:150:              exec_ch_msg/0\r\n/app/workspace/otp_src_27.3.2/lib/ssh/src/ssh_connection.erl:169:                      | exec_ch_msg()\r\n/app/workspace/otp_src_27.3.2/lib/ssh/src/ssh_connection.erl:218:A remote execution can terminate violently because of a signal. Then this\r\n/app/workspace/otp_src_27.3.2/lib/ssh/src/ssh_connection.erl:319:This message requests that the server starts execution of the given command.\r\n/app/workspace/otp_src_27.3.2/lib/ssh/src/ssh_connection.erl:320:This event is sent as a result of calling [ssh_connection:exec/4 ](`exec/4`).\r\n/app/workspace/otp_src_27.3.2/lib/ssh/src/ssh_connection.erl:324:-type exec_ch_msg() :: {exec,\r\n/app/workspace/otp_src_27.3.2/lib/ssh/src/ssh_connection.erl:343:%% remote execution of a program. The program may be a shell, an\r\n/app/workspace/otp_src_27.3.2/lib/ssh/src/ssh_connection.erl:393:%% execution of the given command. \r\n/app/workspace/otp_src_27.3.2/lib/ssh/src/ssh_connection.erl:397:executing the given command. The result is several messages according to the\r\n/app/workspace/otp_src_27.3.2/lib/ssh/src/ssh_connection.erl:398:following pattern. The last message is a channel close message, as the `exec`\r\n/app/workspace/otp_src_27.3.2/lib/ssh/src/ssh_connection.erl:399:request is a one-time execution that closes the channel when it is done.\r\n/app/workspace/otp_src_27.3.2/lib/ssh/src/ssh_connection.erl:401:- **N x [data message(s)](`t:data_ch_msg/0`)** - The result of executing the\r\n/app/workspace/otp_src_27.3.2/lib/ssh/src/ssh_connection.erl:415:  `ssh_client_channel` started for the execution of the command has now been\r\n/app/workspace/otp_src_27.3.2/lib/ssh/src/ssh_connection.erl:419:[One-Time Execution](using_ssh.md#one-time-execution) for examples.\r\n/app/workspace/otp_src_27.3.2/lib/ssh/src/ssh_connection.erl:421:-spec exec(ConnectionRef, ChannelId, Command, Timeout) -> result() when\r\n/app/workspace/otp_src_27.3.2/lib/ssh/src/ssh_connection.erl:427:exec(ConnectionRef, ChannelId, Command, TimeOut) ->\r\n/app/workspace/otp_src_27.3.2/lib/ssh/src/ssh_connection.erl:428:    ssh_connection_handler:request(ConnectionRef, self(), ChannelId, \"exec\",\r\n/app/workspace/otp_src_27.3.2/lib/ssh/src/ssh_connection.erl:438:shell (typically defined in /etc/passwd in Unix systems) is executed at the\r\n/app/workspace/otp_src_27.3.2/lib/ssh/src/ssh_connection.erl:458:Is to be called by a client-channel process for requesting to execute a\r\n/app/workspace/otp_src_27.3.2/lib/ssh/src/ssh_connection.erl:462:[send/3,4,5](`send/3`) must be executed in the same process.\r\n/app/workspace/otp_src_27.3.2/lib/ssh/src/ssh_connection.erl:517:The function `subsystem/4` and subsequent calls of `send/3,4,5` must be executed\r\n/app/workspace/otp_src_27.3.2/lib/ssh/src/ssh_connection.erl:725:%%% ssh_connection:send (executed in the ssh_connection_state machine)\r\n/app/workspace/otp_src_27.3.2/lib/ssh/src/ssh_connection.erl:1148:\t\t\t\t    request_type = \"exec\",\r\n"]
